    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change slots into the existing structure cleanly and follows every established convention here:\n\n- **Data table in the right place.** `REGION_TIMEZONE` sits alongside `CITY_REGION` and `REGION_POSTCODES` in `LocalityResolver` \u2014 the single home for region-keyed reference data \u2014 with matching javadoc style.\n- **Logic in the right unit.** The region\u2192timezone lookup lives in `LocalityResolver.timezone(...)`, mirroring the existing `resolve(...)`/`postcodeRange(...)` static accessors, rather than leaking table/map knowledge into the mapper.\n- **No duplication.** `formatTimezone` derives the region by reusing `formatLocality(owner)` instead of re-resolving locality, so the timezone is keyed off the exact same region the `locality` field exposes.\n- **Consistent mapper pattern.** `formatTimezone` is a carbon copy of the other `format*` methods (null guard, `@Named` exclusion from auto-selection, delegate to a util, same doc shape), and the `@Mapping` entry is placed logically right after `locality`.\n- **Schema addition** matches the surrounding read-only derived fields in `openapi.yml`.\n\nNothing is becoming a catch-all and a maintainer would find this entirely natural.",
